        <name>TextTemplate_180_MEDDPICC_Reminders</name>
        <isViewedAsPlainText>true</isViewedAsPlainText>
        <text>&lt;p&gt;As a reminder, we significantly increase our customer retention rate when a health check is performed on the opportunity and account prior to renewal. Risk mitigation can be successfully addressed by leveraging MEDDPICC as a part of the opportunity renewal process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Our process requires that renewals with Day 1 ARR greater than $100k have the MEDDPICC fields completed on the renewal opportunity by the DSA, with input from the TAM. Additionally the RVP will need to review the opportunity and check the MEDDPICC Validated field before the opportunity can be moved to Signed - Paperwork Received. Ideally this process will be performed by the account team--led by the TAM working with the DSA--at least 6 months prior to the renewal date to allow sufficient time to identify and address risk to ensure we are able to secure the upcoming renewal.&lt;/p&gt;</text>
